    card title "Chicken and egg"

B: So strong  (@draw ax who@)pull hands the town to whoever leads. That's grim news for anyone launching a new platform.

Say a newcomer star (@draw p0@)ts with five p (@draw g0 p1 g1 p2 g2 p3 g3 p4 g4 p5 g5 p6 g6 p7 g7 p8 g8 p9 g9 p10 endread@)ercent of the town, the pull still strong. Its share shrinks.

B: Of course: shops won't take an app nobody  (@highlight p10 endread@)carries, and nobody carries an app no shop takes. Chicken and  (@draw chick egg@)egg: each side waits for the other.

    erase chick egg

B: Microso (@fade p0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10 g0 g1 g2 g3 g4 g5 g6 g7 g8 g9 ax to 0.15@)ft lived i (@draw belf@)t. Its Windows phone chief wrote in 2017 that they had paid app makers, even written apps for them, and still had too few users.

    erase belf

    fade p0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10 g0 g1 g2 g3 g4 g5 g6 g7 g8 g9 ax to 1

The usual cure is to pay one side (@draw b_lo b_hi band band_l bread bnote@) to come first. Here, a bonus b for joining, for the first three rounds only.

B: PayPal paid real money around  (@fade p0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10 g0 g1 g2 g3 g4 g5 g6 g7 g8 g9 ax band band_l to 0.15@)2000. Gues (@draw pp@)s: how much did it give each new user for opening an account?

    ask "How many dollars did PayPal pay each new user for opening an account? Click the line." on pp store g voice b
        right: Twenty dollars: close to your ${g:0}.
        wrong: You said ${g:0}; it was $20.

Twenty d (@highlight pp@)ollars, Elon Musk recalls, and twenty more for each friend they brought.

B: Diners Club did the seeding by ha (@draw dc@)nd in 1950: twenty-seven New York restaurants and about two hundred friends.

    erase pp dc

    fade p0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10 g0 g1 g2 g3 g4 g5 g6 g7 g8 g9 ax band band_l to 1

Watch what size does. A sma (@animate b 1 duration 2.5@)ll bonus is wasted: the share rises, then sinks back the moment the money stops.

A big en (@animate b 2.5 duration 2.5 ghost true@)ough one carries it past the tipping point, an (@draw tip tip_l@)d then the loop does the rest. PayPal cut its bonus t (@draw cuts@)o ten dollars, then five, as the network grew.

B: Try it: drag the bonus b and find the smallest one that still tips the town after the money stops.
    explore params ["b"]

    erase cuts p0_ghost p1_ghost p2_ghost p3_ghost p4_ghost p5_ghost p6_ghost p7_ghost p8_ghost p9_ghost p10_ghost g0_ghost g1_ghost g2_ghost g3_ghost g4_ghost g5_ghost g6_ghost g7_ghost g8_ghost g9_ghost

Abo (@animate b 2 duration 1.5@)ut two: below it, the money is wasted; above it, the town tips. So a launch is a race to  (@highlight tip effect pulse@)the tipping point, and paying enough once lets the network pay from then on.

    pause 0.4

## The brake
feedback:
    style: dry
    perfect: You'd make a fine platform strategist.
    good: Most of the network effect, captured.
    poor: Even PayPal needed a few rounds.
    none: Keep both apps open and try again.
