audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    '|a||Why do platforms win so big? Start with the phone in your pocket: it almost certainly runs one of just two systems.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8360
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Android runs about seventy-two percent of the world''s smartphones, and Apple''s iOS nearly all the rest. That''s StatCounter''s count for October 2026.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ijd28g'
    '|b||Your guess. Drag the last bar to the share left for every other system put together.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1nj2g0q'
    '|a||About three hundredths of a percent. Practically nothing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4320
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||And not for want of trying. Microsoft ended its Windows phones in 2019, and BlackBerry switched off its own system in 2022.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1fcg5bo'
    '|a||The obvious answer: the winners simply made better phones.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1jpbmzy'
    '|b||Partly. But a phone is only as good as its apps, and app makers write for the phones people already own.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1isak83'
    '|a||That''s a network effect: a product is worth more the more people use it. Here it runs through a second group: more users draw more app makers, and more apps draw more users. A cross-side network effect.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ga23jv'
    '|b||A business in the middle of such a loop is a two-sided platform, like Harbourtown''s fish-market app. Jean-Charles Rochet and Jean Tirole, and Geoffrey Parker and Marshall Van Alstyne, built its theory in the early 2000s.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1qjn4gc'
    '|b||A loop between two sides can feed on itself. To see where it leads, give Harbourtown two payment apps, HarbourPay and QuayPay, equally good. The numbers are illustrative.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Each round, every shopper and shop picks one app, lumped together to keep it simple. They like an app more when more of the town pays with it, plus a dash of personal taste.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:8e19ql'
    '|a||HarbourPay starts with fifty-five percent of the town''s payments. Each dot is its share in the next round.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ns813f'
    '|b||With a weak pull, taste wins. The lead melts back, and the town settles at about half each.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:qpu3vr'
    '|a||Now strengthen the pull, n: how much an app gains as more of the town joins it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:6vr95f'
    '|a||Your guess first. The pull rises from 0.5 to 2. What happens to HarbourPay''s five-point lead?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:icyk44'
    '|a||Watch the dots.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1640
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||The lead snowballs. Fifty-five becomes sixty, then seventy, and within a few rounds nearly the whole town is on HarbourPay.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Same apps, same quality. A five-point head start decided everything.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:7laxzc'
    '|a||That''s tipping. Past a certain strength, a split market can''t stay split: it falls to one side.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:v262ua'
    '|b||And the middle is a knife edge. Start HarbourPay at forty-five instead, and QuayPay takes the town. Half is the tipping point.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:oe91j6'
    '|a||Just below one, it drifts back; just above, it runs away. One is the knife''s edge, where a lead barely moves.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9600
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Want the rule behind the dots? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:f293yi'
    '|a||Each round, HarbourPay''s new share is one over one plus e to the minus two n, times two times the old share minus one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||At an even split the share is a half, and the next share is a half again: the split is always a resting point.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:jygp01'
    '|a||But the slope there is exactly n. Above one, a small lead comes back bigger every round, so the split can''t hold.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:a3l5h9'
    '|b||So strong pull hands the town to whoever leads. That''s grim news for anyone launching a new platform.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Say a newcomer starts with five percent of the town, the pull still strong. Its share shrinks.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1fuleou'
    '|b||Of course: shops won''t take an app nobody carries, and nobody carries an app no shop takes. Chicken and egg: each side waits for the other.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8280
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1itehwq'
    '|b||Microsoft lived it. Its Windows phone chief wrote in 2017 that they had paid app makers, even written apps for them, and still had too few users.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:jggeu2'
    '|a||The usual cure is to pay one side to come first. Here, a bonus b for joining, for the first three rounds only.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:lnm6bb'
    '|b||PayPal paid real money around 2000. Guess: how much did it give each new user for opening an account?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1lphng3'
    '|b||How many dollars did PayPal pay each new user for opening an account? Click the line.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1nhxkfv'
    '|a||Twenty dollars, Elon Musk recalls, and twenty more for each friend they brought.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5280
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Diners Club did the seeding by hand in 1950: twenty-seven New York restaurants and about two hundred friends.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:epro1y'
    '|a||Watch what size does. A small bonus is wasted: the share rises, then sinks back the moment the money stops.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:c2mven'
    '|a||A big enough one carries it past the tipping point, and then the loop does the rest. PayPal cut its bonus to ten dollars, then five, as the network grew.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:shk8sv'
    '|a||About two: below it, the money is wasted; above it, the town tips. So a launch is a race to the tipping point, and paying enough once lets the network pay from then on.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12880
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So a strong pull and a head start hand one platform the whole town. But that rests on a quiet assumption: everyone uses only one app.':
